/-!
# The tower of finite level crystalline sites, and the ingredients of `R lim`

Continuing `StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/Crystalline/FiniteLevelSite.lean`, which builds the
finite level bases `S_e = Spec(A/p^eA)` and the fully faithful functor `Cris(X/S_e) ⥤ Cris(X/S)`
of [Stacks, Tag 07MV], this file supplies three things that remark needs and that the library did
not have: *continuity* of change of divided power base on the small crystalline site, the
transition functors `Cris(X/S_m) ⥤ Cris(X/S_e)` for `m ≤ e` which make the finite levels a tower,
and `ℕ`-indexed products in the derived category of abelian groups.

## Continuity, and why it matters

Change of divided power base `Cris(X'/S') ⥤ Cris(X/S)` was known to be *cocontinuous*
(`Crystalline.GlobalCrystallineSituation.smallChangeBase_isCocontinuous`), and the inverse image
of the morphism of topoi that cocontinuity produces is the *sheafification* of the restriction of
a sheaf, not the restriction itself.  That is not good enough for `F_e`: the remark restricts `F`
to `Cris(X/S_e)`, and a sheafification would be a different sheaf whose sections one cannot read
off.  Continuity is exactly the statement that the restriction is already a sheaf, and it is
proved here.

The argument is the small-site form of the one already used for the big crystalline site in
`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/Crystalline/FCrystal.lean`.  Two inputs:

* the topology is generated by the families of restrictions of an object to an open cover of its
  ambient scheme (`...SmallSite.restrictCoverage_toGrothendieck`), and change of base leaves the
  ambient scheme and the Cartesian squares of a covering family untouched, so such a family maps
  to a covering family of the image;
* compatible families stay compatible, because an object of `Cris(X/S)` with a morphism into the
  image of an object of `Cris(X/S_e)` acquires an `S_e`-structure by composing, and the
  comparison morphism of the object so rebased is an isomorphism.  The rebasing is
  `Crystalline.GlobalCrystallineSituation.Thickening.ofSquare`; it stays inside the *small* site
  because its map to `X` becomes the map to `X` of the source after composing with `g`, and `g` is
  an open immersion (`Thickening.isCrystalline_ofSquare`).

## Main definitions

* `Crystalline.GlobalCrystallineSituation.CrystallineThickening.smallOfSquare` and
  `smallOfSquareComparison` — the rebasing of an object of `Cris(X/S)` over the image of an object
  of `Cris(X'/S')`, and its comparison morphism.
* `Crystalline.pAdicLevelTransitionScheme` — the transition `S_m ⟶ S_e` of finite level bases.
* `Crystalline.pAdicLevelStepExtend` — the transition functor `Cris(X/S_m) ⥤ Cris(X/S_e)`.
* `Crystalline.pAdicLevelSheafRestriction` and `Crystalline.pAdicLevelStepSheafRestriction` — the
  restriction of an abelian *sheaf* to a finite level, and between two finite levels.
* `Crystalline.pAdicLevelSmallModuleRestriction` — **`F_e`**, the restriction of a sheaf of
  `𝒪_{X/S}`-modules on the small site `Cris(X/S)` to a sheaf of `𝒪_{X/S_e}`-modules on
  `Cris(X/S_e)`.
* `Crystalline.pAdicLevelDerivedGlobalSections` — **`RΓ(Cris(X/S_e), F_e)`**, the term at level
  `e` of the tower of the remark.

## Main results

* `Crystalline.GlobalCrystallineSituation.smallChangeBase_isContinuous` — **change of divided
  power base is continuous on the small crystalline site**, [Stacks, Tag 07KL]; with
  `smallChangeBase_compatiblePreserving` and
  `CrystallineThickening.map_eq_of_smallChangeBase_comm` as its two halves.
* `Crystalline.pAdicLevelExtend_isContinuous` and `Crystalline.pAdicLevelStepExtend_isContinuous`
  — the two cases of it the tower uses.
* `Crystalline.pAdicLevelStepExtendFullyFaithful` — `Cris(X/S_m)` is a full subcategory of
  `Cris(X/S_e)` for `m ≤ e`, so the finite levels form an increasing chain of full subcategories
  of `Cris(X/S)`.
* `Crystalline.closedFiberMap_pAdicLevelTransitionScheme` — the transition `S_m ⟶ S_e` induces the
  identification of the two closed fibres, which is what makes the level situations a tower over
  the *same* `X`.
* `Crystalline.hasProductsOfShape_nat_derivedCategory` and
  `Crystalline.exists_isDerivedLimit_derivedCategory_addCommGrpCat` — `ℕ`-indexed products exist
  in `D(Ab)`, hence so does `R lim` of any `ℕᵒᵖ`-indexed inverse system there, [Stacks, Tag 07KC]
  and [Stacks, Tag 08TC].

## Indexing: `e ≫ 0`

The remark sets `S_e = Spec(A/p^eA)` only "for `e ≫ 0`", and indeed `A/p^eA` is a divided power
ring only when `(p^e) ⊆ I` is preserved by `γ`.  Nothing here is indexed by all of `ℕ`: every
declaration carries the hypothesis `Crystalline.IsPAdicLevel I γ p e` for each level it mentions,
and the transitions carry one for each of `m` and `e`.  `Crystalline.exists_forall_isPAdicLevel`
provides a threshold `N` above which every exponent is a level, so a genuine `ℕᵒᵖ`-indexed
diagram would be the reindexing `n ↦ N + n` of the data here; that reindexing is not performed,
because there is nothing yet to index (see below).

## What is and is not proved

**Not proved, and not stated: the conclusion**
`RΓ(Cris(X/S), F) = R lim_e RΓ(Cris(X/S_e), F_e)`.

What this file adds is the three ingredients the conclusion is *written in terms of*: the terms
`RΓ(Cris(X/S_e), F_e)` now exist as objects of `D⁺(Ab)`
(`Crystalline.pAdicLevelDerivedGlobalSections`) — which needed the sheaf-level `F_e`, which needed
continuity — the sites they are computed on form a tower, and `R lim` of an `ℕᵒᵖ`-indexed system
of such objects exists once the system does.

What is missing is the system: the *arrows* `RΓ(Cris(X/S_{e}), F_{e}) ⟶ RΓ(Cris(X/S_m), F_m)` of
the tower, for `m ≤ e`.  Restriction of sections gives the underived comparison
`Γ(Cris(X/S_e), -) ⟹ ρ ⋙ Γ(Cris(X/S_m), -)`, where `ρ` is
`Crystalline.pAdicLevelStepSheafRestriction`, and `Stacks.DerivedIndexing`'s
`rightDerivedFunctorPlusNatTrans` derives it; but its target is the right derived functor of the
*composite* `ρ ⋙ Γ(Cris(X/S_m), -)`, and identifying that with `ρ` followed by
`RΓ(Cris(X/S_m), -)` is the Leray-type comparison of
`...SmallSite.derivedGlobalSectionsCompIso`, whose hypothesis is that `ρ` carries an injective
abelian sheaf to one with acyclic global sections.  That hypothesis is not available: it is the
first half of the remark's own hint ("suffices to prove this for `F` injective; in this case the
sheaves `F_e` are injective modules too"), and nothing in the library proves it.  No surrogate is
stated in its place.

The remark's other hint — that `Γ(F) = lim_e Γ(F_e)` because any object of `Cris(X/S)` is locally
an object of some `Cris(X/S_e)` — is likewise not proved; it is a statement about local
nilpotence of `p` on the ambient scheme of an object.

Two smaller gaps, both deliberate.  The compatibility `Cris(X/S_m) ⥤ Cris(X/S_e) ⥤ Cris(X/S)` with
`Cris(X/S_m) ⥤ Cris(X/S)` is not stated: change of base composes only up to a canonical
isomorphism (the structure maps are reassociated and `𝟙 X ≫ 𝟙 X` is not `𝟙 X` on the nose), and
nothing here consumes it.  And `R lim` is taken in the full derived category, along Mathlib's
`DerivedCategory.Plus.ι`, because `ℕ`-indexed products in `DerivedCategory.Plus` are not in the
library; `Plus.ι` is fully faithful and triangulated, so no information is lost in the statement.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 07MV](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/07MV)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 07KL](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/07KL)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 07KC](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/07KC)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 08TC](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/08TC)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 07IC](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/07IC)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 00WW](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/00WW)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits AlgebraicGeometry Opposite

universe t v w w' u

namespace Crystalline.GlobalCrystallineSituation

variable {S S' : GlobalCrystallineSituation.{u}} {f : S.S ⟶ S'.S} {g : S.X ⟶ S'.X}
  {h : S.toClosedFiber ≫ DividedPowerScheme.closedFiberMap f = g ≫ S'.toClosedFiber}

namespace Thickening

/-- **The rebasing of a thickening along a morphism into a rebased object is crystalline.**  Its
map to `X` is the map to `X` of the source composed with the structure map of the target, and that
composite becomes the map to `X` of the source after composing with `g`; since `g` is an open
immersion, so is the composite. -/
theorem isCrystalline_ofSquare [IsOpenImmersion g] {A : Thickening S} {B : Thickening S'}
    (hB : Thickening.IsCrystalline B)
    (p : B ⟶ (changeBase S S' f g h).obj A) :
    Thickening.IsCrystalline
      (ofSquare A B.thickening p.targetHom p.sourceHom p.immersion_naturality) := by
  have key : (p.sourceHom ≫ A.toX) ≫ g = B.toX :=
    (Category.assoc _ _ _).trans p.toX_naturality
  have hoi : IsOpenImmersion ((p.sourceHom ≫ A.toX) ≫ g) := by rw [key]; exact hB
  exact IsOpenImmersion.of_comp (p.sourceHom ≫ A.toX) g

end Thickening

variable [IsOpenImmersion g]

namespace CrystallineThickening

open Thickening

/-- **The underlying morphism of the big crystalline category of a morphism into a rebased
object.**  Change of divided power base on the small site is the big-site change of base on
underlying objects, so this is the component of the morphism; stating its type pins the
compatibility `h`, which the small-site functor hides inside a lift. -/
abbrev smallChangeBaseHom {A : CrystallineThickening S} {B : CrystallineThickening S'}
    (p : B ⟶ (smallChangeBase S S' f g h).obj A) :
    B.obj ⟶ (changeBase S S' f g h).obj A.obj := p.hom

/-- **An object of `Cris(X/S)` out of a morphism of `Cris(Y/S')` into the image of one.**  The
underlying thickening of the source, read over the divided power base `S` through the structure
maps of the target, is an object of `Cris(X/S)`; this is
`Crystalline.GlobalCrystallineSituation.Thickening.ofSquare` on the small site. -/
abbrev smallOfSquare {A : CrystallineThickening S} {B : CrystallineThickening S'}
    (p : B ⟶ (smallChangeBase S S' f g h).obj A) : CrystallineThickening S :=
  ⟨ofSquare A.obj B.obj.thickening (smallChangeBaseHom p).targetHom
      (smallChangeBaseHom p).sourceHom (smallChangeBaseHom p).immersion_naturality,
    isCrystalline_ofSquare B.property (smallChangeBaseHom p)⟩

/-- **The comparison morphism of a rebased object of `Cris(X/S)`.**  Change of divided power base
leaves the underlying thickening untouched, so both of its components are identities. -/
abbrev smallOfSquareComparison {A : CrystallineThickening S} {B : CrystallineThickening S'}
    (p : B ⟶ (smallChangeBase S S' f g h).obj A) :
    (smallChangeBase S S' f g h).obj (smallOfSquare p) ⟶ B :=
  ObjectProperty.homMk (X := (smallChangeBase S S' f g h).obj (smallOfSquare p)) (Y := B)
    (ofSquareComparison (smallChangeBaseHom p))

/-- **The comparison morphism of a rebased object of `Cris(X/S)` is an isomorphism.**  It is one
in the big crystalline category, and the inclusion of a full subcategory reflects
isomorphisms. -/
theorem isIso_smallOfSquareComparison {A : CrystallineThickening S}
    {B : CrystallineThickening S'} (p : B ⟶ (smallChangeBase S S' f g h).obj A) :
    IsIso (smallOfSquareComparison p) := by
  have h₁ : IsIso ((ObjectProperty.ι (Thickening.IsCrystalline (S := S'))).map
      (smallOfSquareComparison p)) := isIso_ofSquareComparison (smallChangeBaseHom p)
  exact isIso_of_reflects_iso _ (ObjectProperty.ι (Thickening.IsCrystalline (S := S')))

/-- The underlying identity of a factorization through the image of a morphism of
`Cris(X/S)`, read in the big crystalline category. -/
theorem smallChangeBaseHom_comp {A Y : CrystallineThickening S} (k : Y ⟶ A)
    {B : CrystallineThickening S'} {p : B ⟶ (smallChangeBase S S' f g h).obj A}
    {q : B ⟶ (smallChangeBase S S' f g h).obj Y}
    (hq : q ≫ (smallChangeBase S S' f g h).map k = p) :
    smallChangeBaseHom q ≫ (changeBase S S' f g h).map k.hom = smallChangeBaseHom p :=
  congrArg InducedCategory.Hom.hom hq

/-- The morphism of `Cris(X/S)` factoring the structure morphism of a rebased object through a
morphism of `Cris(X/S)` that the original morphism factors through. -/
abbrev smallOfSquareLift {A Y : CrystallineThickening S} (k : Y ⟶ A)
    {B : CrystallineThickening S'} (p : B ⟶ (smallChangeBase S S' f g h).obj A)
    (q : B ⟶ (smallChangeBase S S' f g h).obj Y)
    (hq : q ≫ (smallChangeBase S S' f g h).map k = p) :
    smallOfSquare p ⟶ Y :=
  ObjectProperty.homMk (X := smallOfSquare p) (Y := Y)
    (ofSquareLift k.hom (smallChangeBaseHom p) (smallChangeBaseHom q)
      (smallChangeBaseHom_comp k hq))

/-- **Sections of a presheaf on `Cris(Y/S')` which agree over `Cris(X/S)` agree over the images
of the two morphisms of a commuting square of `Cris(Y/S')`.**  The vertex of the square, rebased
along its diagonal, is an object of `Cris(X/S)` over which the hypothesis applies, and the
comparison morphism of the rebased vertex is an isomorphism, so it may be cancelled.  This is
`Crystalline.GlobalCrystallineSituation.Thickening.map_eq_of_changeBase_comm` on the small
site. -/
theorem map_eq_of_smallChangeBase_comm {P : (CrystallineThickening S')ᵒᵖ ⥤ Type t}
    {A Y₁ Y₂ : CrystallineThickening S} (k₁ : Y₁ ⟶ A) (k₂ : Y₂ ⟶ A)
    {B : CrystallineThickening S'}
    (q₁ : B ⟶ (smallChangeBase S S' f g h).obj Y₁)
    (q₂ : B ⟶ (smallChangeBase S S' f g h).obj Y₂)
    (hq : q₁ ≫ (smallChangeBase S S' f g h).map k₁ =
      q₂ ≫ (smallChangeBase S S' f g h).map k₂)
    {y₁ : P.obj (op ((smallChangeBase S S' f g h).obj Y₁))}
    {y₂ : P.obj (op ((smallChangeBase S S' f g h).obj Y₂))}
    (hy : ∀ (Z : CrystallineThickening S) (m₁ : Z ⟶ Y₁) (m₂ : Z ⟶ Y₂), m₁ ≫ k₁ = m₂ ≫ k₂ →
      P.map ((smallChangeBase S S' f g h).map m₁).op y₁ =
        P.map ((smallChangeBase S S' f g h).map m₂).op y₂) :
    P.map q₁.op y₁ = P.map q₂.op y₂ := by
  obtain ⟨p, hp⟩ : ∃ p, q₁ ≫ (smallChangeBase S S' f g h).map k₁ = p := ⟨_, rfl⟩
  have hp' : q₂ ≫ (smallChangeBase S S' f g h).map k₂ = p := hq.symm.trans hp
  have key := hy _ (smallOfSquareLift k₁ p q₁ hp) (smallOfSquareLift k₂ p q₂ hp')
    (ObjectProperty.hom_ext _
      ((ofSquareLift_comp k₁.hom _ _ (smallChangeBaseHom_comp k₁ hp)).trans
        (ofSquareLift_comp k₂.hom _ _ (smallChangeBaseHom_comp k₂ hp')).symm))
  have hmap : ∀ (Y : CrystallineThickening S) (k : Y ⟶ A)
      (q : B ⟶ (smallChangeBase S S' f g h).obj Y)
      (hqk : q ≫ (smallChangeBase S S' f g h).map k = p),
      (smallChangeBase S S' f g h).map (smallOfSquareLift k p q hqk) =
        smallOfSquareComparison p ≫ q := fun Y k q hqk ↦
    ObjectProperty.hom_ext _
      (changeBase_map_ofSquareLift k.hom _ _ (smallChangeBaseHom_comp k hqk))
  rw [hmap _ k₁ q₁ hp, hmap _ k₂ q₂ hp'] at key
  have hgoal : P.map (smallOfSquareComparison p).op (P.map q₁.op y₁) =
      P.map (smallOfSquareComparison p).op (P.map q₂.op y₂) := by
    simpa only [op_comp, Functor.map_comp, types_comp_apply] using key
  have := isIso_smallOfSquareComparison p
  exact (P.mapIso (asIso (smallOfSquareComparison p)).op).toEquiv.injective hgoal

end CrystallineThickening

open CrystallineThickening

/-- **Change of divided power base turns compatible families of sections on the small crystalline
site into compatible families.** -/
theorem smallChangeBase_compatiblePreserving :
    CompatiblePreserving.{t} (smallTopology S') (smallChangeBase S S' f g h) where
  compatible := by
    intro P Z T x hx Y₁ Y₂ W q₁ q₂ k₁ k₂ hk₁ hk₂ hq
    exact map_eq_of_smallChangeBase_comm k₁ k₂ q₁ q₂ hq fun _ m₁ m₂ hm ↦ hx m₁ m₂ hk₁ hk₂ hm

/-- **Stacks Project, Tag 07KL.**  Change of divided power base is *continuous* for the Zariski
topologies of the small crystalline sites.  The topology is generated by the families of
restrictions of an object to an open cover of its ambient scheme, and change of base leaves the
ambient scheme and the Cartesian squares untouched, so such a family maps to a covering family of
the image; the sheaf condition then transfers because change of base turns compatible families
into compatible families.

Together with
`Crystalline.GlobalCrystallineSituation.smallChangeBase_isCocontinuous` this makes change of base
a morphism of sites in both directions; the point of continuity is that the *restriction* of a
sheaf along change of base is again a sheaf, so the pullback of sheaves is restriction on the nose
rather than its sheafification. -/
@[stacks 07KL "the functor is continuous"]
instance smallChangeBase_isContinuous :
    (smallChangeBase S S' f g h).IsContinuous (smallTopology S) (smallTopology S') where
  op_comp_isSheaf_of_types G := by
    rw [← SmallSite.restrictCoverage_toGrothendieck, Presieve.isSheaf_coverage]
    rintro A R ⟨I, V, hV, rfl⟩
    have hE : CrystallineThickening.IsZariskiCovering (A.restrictOpenCover V) :=
      CrystallineThickening.isZariskiCovering_restrictOpenCover A V hV
    have hEF : CrystallineThickening.IsZariskiCovering
        ((A.restrictOpenCover V).map (smallChangeBase S S' f g h)) := ⟨hE.1, hE.2⟩
    have hsheaf : Presieve.IsSheafFor G.obj
        (((A.restrictOpenCover V).map (smallChangeBase S S' f g h)).presieve₀ :
          Presieve ((smallChangeBase S S' f g h).obj A)) :=
      (Presieve.isSheafFor_iff_generate _).2
        ((isSheaf_iff_isSheaf_of_type _ _).1 G.property _
          (smallZariskiCovering_mem_smallTopology S' _ hEF))
    have hpreF : (((A.restrictOpenCover V).map (smallChangeBase S S' f g h)).presieve₀ :
          Presieve ((smallChangeBase S S' f g h).obj A)) =
        Presieve.ofArrows
          (fun i ↦ (smallChangeBase S S' f g h).obj ((A.restrictOpenCover V).X i))
          (fun i ↦ (smallChangeBase S S' f g h).map ((A.restrictOpenCover V).f i)) := rfl
    have hpre : ((A.restrictOpenCover V).presieve₀ : Presieve A) =
        Presieve.ofArrows (A.restrictOpenCover V).X (A.restrictOpenCover V).f := rfl
    rw [hpreF, Presieve.isSheafFor_arrows_iff] at hsheaf
    rw [hpre, Presieve.isSheafFor_arrows_iff]
    intro x hx
    exact hsheaf x fun i j W q₁ q₂ hq ↦
      map_eq_of_smallChangeBase_comm _ _ q₁ q₂ hq fun Z m₁ m₂ hm ↦ hx i j Z m₁ m₂ hm

end Crystalline.GlobalCrystallineSituation

/-! ### The tower of finite level sites -/

namespace Crystalline

open DividedPowerScheme GlobalCrystallineSituation

section Level

attribute [local implicit_reducible] DividedPowerScheme.specDividedPowerScheme

variable {A : Type u} [CommRing A] (I : Ideal A) (γ : DividedPowers I) (p : ℕ)

/-- **The transition morphism `A/p^eA → A/p^mA` of finite divided power levels is surjective**, the
two rings being quotients of `A` and the morphism being compatible with the quotient maps. -/
theorem pAdicLevelTransition_surjective {m e : ℕ} (hm : IsPAdicLevel I γ p m)
    (he : IsPAdicLevel I γ p e) (hme : m ≤ e) :
    Function.Surjective (pAdicLevelTransition I γ p hm he hme).toRingHom := by
  intro x
  obtain ⟨a, rfl⟩ := Ideal.Quotient.mk_surjective x
  exact ⟨Ideal.Quotient.mk _ a, rfl⟩

/-- **The transition `S_m ⟶ S_e` of finite level bases**, for `m ≤ e`: `Spec` of the canonical
surjection `A/p^eA → A/p^mA` of divided power rings.  Note the direction: the *smaller* level is
the *closed* subscheme, so `Cris(X/S_m)` will sit inside `Cris(X/S_e)`. -/
def pAdicLevelTransitionScheme {m e : ℕ} (hm : IsPAdicLevel I γ p m) (he : IsPAdicLevel I γ p e)
    (hme : m ≤ e) : pAdicLevelScheme I γ p hm ⟶ pAdicLevelScheme I γ p he :=
  specDividedPowerMap (pAdicLevelTransition I γ p hm he hme)

/-- The underlying morphism of schemes of `pAdicLevelTransitionScheme` is `Spec.map` of the ring
map `A/p^eA → A/p^mA`. -/
@[simp]
theorem pAdicLevelTransitionScheme_hom {m e : ℕ} (hm : IsPAdicLevel I γ p m)
    (he : IsPAdicLevel I γ p e) (hme : m ≤ e) :
    (pAdicLevelTransitionScheme I γ p hm he hme).hom =
      Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (pAdicLevelTransition I γ p hm he hme).toRingHom) := rfl

/-- **The transition `S_m ⟶ S_e` is a closed immersion**, being `Spec` of a surjection. -/
instance isClosedImmersion_pAdicLevelTransitionScheme_hom {m e : ℕ}
    (hm : IsPAdicLevel I γ p m) (he : IsPAdicLevel I γ p e) (hme : m ≤ e) :
    IsClosedImmersion (pAdicLevelTransitionScheme I γ p hm he hme).hom := by
  rw [pAdicLevelTransitionScheme_hom]
  exact IsClosedImmersion.spec_of_surjective _ (pAdicLevelTransition_surjective I γ p hm he hme)

/-- **The finite level bases form a tower under `S`.**  Descending from `S` to level `e` and then
to level `m ≤ e` is descending from `S` to level `m`; this is
`Crystalline.pAdicLevelProj_comp_pAdicLevelTransition` after `Spec`. -/
@[reassoc]
theorem pAdicLevelTransitionScheme_comp_proj {m e : ℕ} (hm : IsPAdicLevel I γ p m)
    (he : IsPAdicLevel I γ p e) (hme : m ≤ e) :
    pAdicLevelTransitionScheme I γ p hm he hme ≫ pAdicLevelSchemeProj I γ p he =
      pAdicLevelSchemeProj I γ p hm := by
  have h₁ : specDividedPowerMap
        (pAdicLevelProj I γ p he ≫ pAdicLevelTransition I γ p hm he hme) =
      pAdicLevelTransitionScheme I γ p hm he hme ≫ pAdicLevelSchemeProj I γ p he :=
    DividedPowerScheme.specDividedPowerMap_comp _ _
  rw [← h₁, pAdicLevelProj_comp_pAdicLevelTransition]
  rfl

/-- **The transition `S_m ⟶ S_e` induces, on closed fibres, the identification of the closed fibre
of `S_m` with that of `S_e`** — both being the closed fibre `S_0 = Spec(A/I)` of `S`.  This is what
makes the level situations a tower over the *same* `X`. -/
theorem closedFiberMap_pAdicLevelTransitionScheme {m e : ℕ} (hm : IsPAdicLevel I γ p m)
    (he : IsPAdicLevel I γ p e) (hme : m ≤ e) :
    closedFiberMap (pAdicLevelTransitionScheme I γ p hm he hme) =
      (pAdicLevelClosedFiberIso I γ p hm).hom ≫ (pAdicLevelClosedFiberIso I γ p he).inv := by
  rw [Iso.eq_comp_inv, pAdicLevelClosedFiberIso_hom_eq, pAdicLevelClosedFiberIso_hom_eq,
    ← closedFiberMap_comp, pAdicLevelTransitionScheme_comp_proj]

variable [Fact p.Prime] [Algebra (DividedPowers.IntegersAtPrime p) A]

/-- **The compatibility of the transition `S_m ⟶ S_e` with the structure morphisms**, the
hypothesis of change of divided power base for the pair `(S_m ⟶ S_e, 𝟙 X)`. -/
theorem pAdicLevelStep_changeBase_condition {m e : ℕ} (hm : IsPAdicLevel I γ p m)
    (he : IsPAdicLevel I γ p e) (hme : m ≤ e) (X : Scheme.{u})
    (toCF : X ⟶ closedFiber (specBase I γ))
    (hX : ∀ x : X, IsNilpotent (p : X.presheaf.stalk x)) :
    (pAdicLevelSituation I γ p hm X toCF hX).toClosedFiber ≫
        closedFiberMap (pAdicLevelTransitionScheme I γ p hm he hme) =
      (𝟙 X : X ⟶ X) ≫ (pAdicLevelSituation I γ p he X toCF hX).toClosedFiber := by
  change (toCF ≫ (pAdicLevelClosedFiberIso I γ p hm).inv) ≫
      closedFiberMap (pAdicLevelTransitionScheme I γ p hm he hme) =
    (𝟙 X : X ⟶ X) ≫ toCF ≫ (pAdicLevelClosedFiberIso I γ p he).inv
  rw [closedFiberMap_pAdicLevelTransitionScheme, Category.assoc, Iso.inv_hom_id_assoc,
    Category.id_comp]

/-- The identity of `X`, read as a morphism from the thickened space of `X/S_m` to that of
`X/S_e`, is an open immersion. -/
instance isOpenImmersion_pAdicLevelStepId {m e : ℕ} (hm : IsPAdicLevel I γ p m)
    (he : IsPAdicLevel I γ p e) (X : Scheme.{u})
    (toCF : X ⟶ closedFiber (specBase I γ))
    (hX : ∀ x : X, IsNilpotent (p : X.presheaf.stalk x)) :
    @IsOpenImmersion (pAdicLevelSituation I γ p hm X toCF hX).X
      (pAdicLevelSituation I γ p he X toCF hX).X (𝟙 X) :=
  inferInstanceAs (IsOpenImmersion (𝟙 X))

/-- **Stacks Project, Tag 07MV.**  The transition functor `Cris(X/S_m) ⥤ Cris(X/S_e)` of the tower
of finite divided power levels, for `m ≤ e`: change of divided power base along the closed
immersion `S_m ⟶ S_e` and the identity of `X`.  This is the arrow of the tower whose inverse
limit the remark takes; `Crystalline.pAdicLevelExtend` is its colimit end, the functor
to `Cris(X/S)` itself. -/
@[stacks 07MV "the transition functor Cris(X/S_m) ⥤ Cris(X/S_e) of the tower of finite levels"]
def pAdicLevelStepExtend {m e : ℕ} (hm : IsPAdicLevel I γ p m) (he : IsPAdicLevel I γ p e)
    (hme : m ≤ e) (X : Scheme.{u}) (toCF : X ⟶ closedFiber (specBase I γ))
    (hX : ∀ x : X, IsNilpotent (p : X.presheaf.stalk x)) :
    GlobalCrystallineSituation.CrystallineThickening
        (pAdicLevelSituation I γ p hm X toCF hX) ⥤
      GlobalCrystallineSituation.CrystallineThickening
        (pAdicLevelSituation I γ p he X toCF hX) :=
  GlobalCrystallineSituation.smallChangeBase _ _
    (pAdicLevelTransitionScheme I γ p hm he hme) (𝟙 X)
    (pAdicLevelStep_changeBase_condition I γ p hm he hme X toCF hX)

/-- **Stacks Project, Tag 07MV.**  `Cris(X/S_m)` is a full subcategory of `Cris(X/S_e)` for
`m ≤ e`: the transition `S_m ⟶ S_e` is a closed immersion, hence a monomorphism. -/
@[stacks 07MV "Cris(X/S_m) is a full subcategory of Cris(X/S_e) for m ≤ e"]
def pAdicLevelStepExtendFullyFaithful {m e : ℕ} (hm : IsPAdicLevel I γ p m)
    (he : IsPAdicLevel I γ p e) (hme : m ≤ e) (X : Scheme.{u})
    (toCF : X ⟶ closedFiber (specBase I γ))
    (hX : ∀ x : X, IsNilpotent (p : X.presheaf.stalk x)) :
    (pAdicLevelStepExtend I γ p hm he hme X toCF hX).FullyFaithful :=
  GlobalCrystallineSituation.smallChangeBaseFullyFaithfulOfMono
    (S := pAdicLevelSituation I γ p hm X toCF hX)
    (S' := pAdicLevelSituation I γ p he X toCF hX)
    (f := pAdicLevelTransitionScheme I γ p hm he hme) (g := 𝟙 X)
    (h := pAdicLevelStep_changeBase_condition I γ p hm he hme X toCF hX)
    (DividedPowerScheme.mono_of_mono_hom
      (inferInstanceAs (Mono (pAdicLevelTransitionScheme I γ p hm he hme).hom)))

/-- **The transition functor of the tower of finite levels is continuous**, so restriction of
sheaves along it is restriction on the nose. -/
instance pAdicLevelStepExtend_isContinuous {m e : ℕ} (hm : IsPAdicLevel I γ p m)
    (he : IsPAdicLevel I γ p e) (hme : m ≤ e) (X : Scheme.{u})
    (toCF : X ⟶ closedFiber (specBase I γ))
    (hX : ∀ x : X, IsNilpotent (p : X.presheaf.stalk x)) :
    (pAdicLevelStepExtend I γ p hm he hme X toCF hX).IsContinuous
      (GlobalCrystallineSituation.smallTopology (pAdicLevelSituation I γ p hm X toCF hX))
      (GlobalCrystallineSituation.smallTopology (pAdicLevelSituation I γ p he X toCF hX)) :=
  GlobalCrystallineSituation.smallChangeBase_isContinuous

/-- **The functor `Cris(X/S_e) ⥤ Cris(X/S)` is continuous.**  This is the missing half of
[Stacks, Tag 07KL] for the small site, proved in
`Crystalline.GlobalCrystallineSituation.smallChangeBase_isContinuous`; cocontinuity alone gives a
pullback of sheaves that is only the *sheafification* of the restriction. -/
instance pAdicLevelExtend_isContinuous {e : ℕ} (he : IsPAdicLevel I γ p e) (X : Scheme.{u})
    (toCF : X ⟶ closedFiber (specBase I γ))
    (hX : ∀ x : X, IsNilpotent (p : X.presheaf.stalk x)) :
    (pAdicLevelExtend I γ p he X toCF hX).IsContinuous
      (GlobalCrystallineSituation.smallTopology (pAdicLevelSituation I γ p he X toCF hX))
      (GlobalCrystallineSituation.smallTopology (specSituation I γ p X toCF hX)) :=
  GlobalCrystallineSituation.smallChangeBase_isContinuous

/-! ### The sheaf-level restriction `F_e` -/

/-- **The restriction of an abelian sheaf on `Cris(X/S)` to `Cris(X/S_e)`.**  Because
`Crystalline.pAdicLevelExtend` is continuous, the restriction of a sheaf along it is again a
sheaf, so this is restriction on the nose and not a sheafification. -/
def pAdicLevelSheafRestriction {e : ℕ} (he : IsPAdicLevel I γ p e) (X : Scheme.{u})
    (toCF : X ⟶ closedFiber (specBase I γ))
    (hX : ∀ x : X, IsNilpotent (p : X.presheaf.stalk x)) :
    Sheaf (GlobalCrystallineSituation.smallTopology (specSituation I γ p X toCF hX))
        AddCommGrpCat.{u + 1} ⥤
      Sheaf (GlobalCrystallineSituation.smallTopology
        (pAdicLevelSituation I γ p he X toCF hX)) AddCommGrpCat.{u + 1} :=
  (pAdicLevelExtend I γ p he X toCF hX).sheafPushforwardContinuous AddCommGrpCat.{u + 1} _ _

/-- **Restriction along `Cris(X/S_e) ⥤ Cris(X/S)` carries `𝒪_{X/S}` to `𝒪_{X/S_e}` on the
nose**, so the comparison morphism of structure sheaves is the identity; this is
`Crystalline.pAdicLevelExtend_op_comp_crisRing` read on sheaves. -/
def pAdicLevelSmallStructureHom {e : ℕ} (he : IsPAdicLevel I γ p e) (X : Scheme.{u})
    (toCF : X ⟶ closedFiber (specBase I γ))
    (hX : ∀ x : X, IsNilpotent (p : X.presheaf.stalk x)) :
    GlobalCrystallineSituation.SmallSite.structureSheaf
        (pAdicLevelSituation I γ p he X toCF hX) ⟶
      ((pAdicLevelExtend I γ p he X toCF hX).sheafPushforwardContinuous RingCat.{u} _ _).obj
        (GlobalCrystallineSituation.SmallSite.structureSheaf
          (specSituation I γ p X toCF hX)) :=
  ⟨𝟙 _⟩

/-- **Stacks Project, Tag 07MV.**  `F_e`, the restriction of a sheaf of `𝒪_{X/S}`-modules on the
small crystalline site `Cris(X/S)` to a sheaf of `𝒪_{X/S_e}`-modules on `Cris(X/S_e)`.

This is the `F_e` of the remark.  It is the restriction itself, not a sheafification of it: that
rests on the continuity of `Crystalline.pAdicLevelExtend`, and no comparison of structure sheaves
is needed because the restriction of `𝒪_{X/S}` along the functor *is* `𝒪_{X/S_e}`. -/
@[stacks 07MV
  "F_e as a sheaf of 𝒪_{X/S_e}-modules on the small site Cris(X/S_e), by restriction"]
def pAdicLevelSmallModuleRestriction {e : ℕ} (he : IsPAdicLevel I γ p e) (X : Scheme.{u})
    (toCF : X ⟶ closedFiber (specBase I γ))
    (hX : ∀ x : X, IsNilpotent (p : X.presheaf.stalk x)) :
    SheafOfModules.{u} (GlobalCrystallineSituation.SmallSite.structureSheaf
        (specSituation I γ p X toCF hX)) ⥤
      SheafOfModules.{u} (GlobalCrystallineSituation.SmallSite.structureSheaf
        (pAdicLevelSituation I γ p he X toCF hX)) :=
  SheafOfModules.pushforward (pAdicLevelSmallStructureHom I γ p he X toCF hX)

/-- **The restriction of an abelian sheaf to a finite level, through an intermediate level.**
Restricting from `Cris(X/S)` to `Cris(X/S_e)` and then to `Cris(X/S_m)` is restriction along the
composite functor; the two restrictions compose on the nose, by
`CategoryTheory.Functor.sheafPushforwardContinuousComp`. -/
def pAdicLevelStepSheafRestriction {m e : ℕ} (hm : IsPAdicLevel I γ p m)
    (he : IsPAdicLevel I γ p e) (hme : m ≤ e) (X : Scheme.{u})
    (toCF : X ⟶ closedFiber (specBase I γ))
    (hX : ∀ x : X, IsNilpotent (p : X.presheaf.stalk x)) :
    Sheaf (GlobalCrystallineSituation.smallTopology
        (pAdicLevelSituation I γ p he X toCF hX)) AddCommGrpCat.{u + 1} ⥤
      Sheaf (GlobalCrystallineSituation.smallTopology
        (pAdicLevelSituation I γ p hm X toCF hX)) AddCommGrpCat.{u + 1} :=
  (pAdicLevelStepExtend I γ p hm he hme X toCF hX).sheafPushforwardContinuous
    AddCommGrpCat.{u + 1} _ _

/-! ### Derived global sections at a finite level, and `R lim` -/

/-- **Stacks Project, Tag 07MV.**  `RΓ(Cris(X/S_e), F_e)`, the term at level `e` of the tower
whose derived inverse limit the remark takes: derived global sections on the small crystalline
site of `X/S_e` applied to the restriction `F_e` of an abelian sheaf `F` on `Cris(X/S)`.

This is an object of `D⁺(Ab)`, and it is the restriction `F_e` itself — not a sheafification of
it — that is being evaluated, by the continuity of `Crystalline.pAdicLevelExtend`. -/
@[stacks 07MV
  "the individual terms RΓ(Cris(X/S_e), F_e) of the remark's R lim, for F an abelian sheaf; \
   NOT the tower (its arrows are missing) and NOT the conclusion"]
def pAdicLevelDerivedGlobalSections {e : ℕ} (he : IsPAdicLevel I γ p e) (X : Scheme.{u})
    (toCF : X ⟶ closedFiber (specBase I γ))
    (hX : ∀ x : X, IsNilpotent (p : X.presheaf.stalk x))
    [HasDerivedCategory.{w} (Sheaf (GlobalCrystallineSituation.smallTopology
      (pAdicLevelSituation I γ p he X toCF hX)) AddCommGrpCat.{u + 1})]
    [HasDerivedCategory.{w'} AddCommGrpCat.{u + 1}]
    (F : Sheaf (GlobalCrystallineSituation.smallTopology (specSituation I γ p X toCF hX))
      AddCommGrpCat.{u + 1}) :
    DerivedCategory.Plus AddCommGrpCat.{u + 1} :=
  (GlobalCrystallineSituation.SmallSite.derivedGlobalSections
      (pAdicLevelSituation I γ p he X toCF hX)).obj
    ((pAdicLevelSheafRestriction I γ p he X toCF hX).obj F)

end Level

/-- **Products indexed by `ℕ` exist in the derived category of abelian groups.**  This is
[Stacks, Tag 07KC] for `AddCommGrpCat`: countable products of abelian groups are exact
(`CategoryTheory.HasExactLimitsOfShape` for a discrete shape, from Mathlib's `AB` file), which is
the hypothesis of `Stacks.DerivedProducts.hasProductsOfShape_nat`. -/
instance hasProductsOfShape_nat_derivedCategory
    [HasDerivedCategory.{w} AddCommGrpCat.{v}] :
    HasProductsOfShape ℕ (DerivedCategory AddCommGrpCat.{v}) :=
  Stacks.DerivedProducts.hasProductsOfShape_nat

/-- **Every `ℕᵒᵖ`-indexed inverse system in the derived category of abelian groups has a derived
limit `R lim`.**  Products of shape `ℕ` exist there by
`Crystalline.hasProductsOfShape_nat_derivedCategory`, which is all that
`CategoryTheory.Pretriangulated.exists_isDerivedLimit` ([Stacks, Tag 08TC]) needs.

This is the right-hand side of [Stacks, Tag 07MV] once the tower is in hand: a tower of the
objects `RΓ(Cris(X/S_e), F_e)` of `Crystalline.pAdicLevelDerivedGlobalSections` is read in the
full derived category along Mathlib's `DerivedCategory.Plus.ι` — the bounded below derived
category itself is not known to have `ℕ`-indexed products — and then has a derived limit. -/
theorem exists_isDerivedLimit_derivedCategory_addCommGrpCat
    [HasDerivedCategory.{w} AddCommGrpCat.{v}]
    (T : ℕᵒᵖ ⥤ DerivedCategory AddCommGrpCat.{v}) :
    ∃ K, CategoryTheory.Pretriangulated.IsDerivedLimit T K :=
  CategoryTheory.Pretriangulated.exists_isDerivedLimit T

end Crystalline

end
